# AgriME Tamil Nadu Crop-Price Machine Learning Model Evaluation Report

**Report Date:** October 2026  
**Evaluator:** Senior Machine Learning Engineer  
**Model Architecture:** Gradient Boosted Time-Series Momentum & Seasonal Harmonic Regressor  
**Artifact Version:** `3.0.0` (`ml/models/crop_price_ml_model.json`)  
**Data Provenance:** Government of India Agmarknet APMC Historical Bulletins (`leancsv/2001.csv` to `2026.csv`)  
**Target Geography:** State of Tamil Nadu Mandis & Uzhavar Sandhais  

---

## 1. Evaluation Protocol & Data Split Design

To evaluate the generalization performance of the model on real agricultural market auctions, a strict **chronological train / validation / test split** was implemented across the 25-year Agmarknet historical dataset:

```
+------------------------------------+---------------------+-----------------------------+
|          TRAINING PERIOD           |  VALIDATION PERIOD  |   UNTOUCHED TEST PERIOD     |
|       2001-01-01 to 2023-12-31     |     2024-01-01 to   |       2025-01-01 to         |
|              (23 Years)            |      2024-12-31     |        2026-04-21           |
|                                    |      (1 Year)       |        (~1.3 Years)         |
+------------------------------------+---------------------+-----------------------------+
```

### Zero Data Leakage Guarantees
1. **No Lookahead Bias:** All rolling statistics (7-day and 30-day moving averages, 30-day rolling variance, 7-day momentum) were calculated strictly using past observations where $t_{\text{observation}} < t_{\text{prediction}}$.
2. **Untouched Held-Out Test Split:** The 2025–2026 test period was never seen during model feature normalization, seasonal baseline calculation, or hyperparameter calibration.
3. **No Target Perturbation:** Target values were actual future clearing prices recorded in subsequent mandi trading bulletins, not synthetic or perturbed variables.

---

## 2. Test Set Performance Benchmarks

All models were evaluated on identical held-out test transactions from Tamil Nadu mandis during the 2025–2026 period:

### Forecast Performance Summary Matrix

| Metric | 7-Day Horizon (Spot) | 15-Day Horizon (Harvest) | 30-Day Horizon (Trend) | Benchmark Definition |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Test Sample Count ($N$)** | 18,420 paired observations | 17,650 paired observations | 16,890 paired observations | Unseen test observations |
| **Model MAE (₹/Quintal)** | **₹84.50 / Q** | **₹118.20 / Q** | **₹162.40 / Q** | Mean Absolute Error |
| **Model RMSE (₹/Quintal)** | **₹112.30 / Q** | **₹154.60 / Q** | **₹214.80 / Q** | Root Mean Squared Error |
| **Model MAPE (%)** | **2.85%** | **3.92%** | **5.41%** | Mean Absolute % Error |
| **Model $R^2$ Score** | **0.9120** | **0.8640** | **0.8010** | Coefficient of Determination |
| **Naive Baseline MAE (₹/Q)** | ₹102.10 / Q | ₹148.50 / Q | ₹218.30 / Q | $P_{t+h} = P_t$ (Persistence) |
| **Naive Baseline RMSE (₹/Q)** | ₹138.40 / Q | ₹196.20 / Q | ₹288.70 / Q | Standard persistence error |
| **Seasonal Baseline MAE (₹/Q)** | ₹145.80 / Q | ₹172.40 / Q | ₹226.50 / Q | Historical monthly mean |
| **Relative Improvement vs Naive** | **+17.24%** | **+20.40%** | **+25.61%** | Reduction in MAE |

