## 3. Commodity-Wise Breakdown in Tamil Nadu

| Commodity | Historical Category | 15-Day Test MAE (₹/Q) | 15-Day Test RMSE (₹/Q) | Volatility & Dynamics Analysis |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Paddy (Dhan Common)** | Cereal / Staple | ₹58.20 / Q | ₹76.40 / Q | High stability anchored by Minimum Support Price (MSP) and Civil Supplies procurement. |
| **Maize** | Feed / Grain | ₹72.10 / Q | ₹94.50 / Q | Moderate volatility correlated with poultry feed demand in Namakkal district. |
| **Cotton** | Fiber / Cash Crop | ₹185.00 / Q | ₹240.20 / Q | Higher price scale (~₹7,000/Q); low percentage error (~2.6%). |
| **Groundnut** | Oilseed | ₹142.30 / Q | ₹188.50 / Q | Steady post-harvest trading with seasonal monsoon sowing premiums. |
| **Tomato** | Highly Perishable | ₹168.40 / Q | ₹228.10 / Q | High seasonal elasticity; 7-day momentum features capture rapid supply gluts. |
| **Onion (Bellary/Small)** | Semi-perishable | ₹136.50 / Q | ₹182.00 / Q | Storage depletion spikes in pre-monsoon months successfully modeled by harmonic cycles. |
| **Banana (Green)** | Horticulture | ₹88.20 / Q | ₹116.40 / Q | Consistent year-round arrivals in Trichy and Theni mandis. |
| **Turmeric** | Commercial Spice | ₹210.50 / Q | ₹275.00 / Q | High value (~₹12,000/Q); strong multi-month cyclical pattern in Erode mandi. |

---

## 4. Empirical Prediction Intervals (Confidence Bands)

Rather than assuming theoretical Gaussian error distributions, the prediction intervals are empirically calibrated from the held-out validation and test Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE):

$$\text{Prediction Interval} = \left[ \max(50, \hat{P} - 1.96 \cdot \text{RMSE}_h), \quad \hat{P} + 1.96 \cdot \text{RMSE}_h \right]$$

- **7-Day Horizon:** Margin of error $\approx \pm ₹220/\text{Q}$ ($\pm ₹2.20/\text{kg}$).
- **15-Day Horizon:** Margin of error $\approx \pm ₹303/\text{Q}$ ($\pm ₹3.03/\text{kg}$).
- **30-Day Horizon:** Margin of error $\approx \pm ₹421/\text{Q}$ ($\pm ₹4.21/\text{kg}$).

---

## 5. Practical Significance for Farmers and Traders

1. **Spot Decision Support:** With a 7-day MAE of ₹84.50/Q (< 3% error), farmers can decide whether to harvest and transport produce today or hold for 3–5 days to capture projected mandi price rises.
2. **Transportation & Inter-Mandi Arbitrage:** Comparing predictions across neighboring mandis (e.g., Vellore vs Ranipet vs Tiruvannamalai) enables farmers to select higher-clearing markets that offset transport costs.
3. **Transparent Uncertainty:** The UI displays explicit $\text{Min} \leftrightarrow \text{Max}$ ranges alongside point forecasts, preventing overconfidence during market shocks.
